amino acid hypervariable domain that is recognized by the human immune response</article-title><source>Microbiology</source><year>1997</year><volume>143</volume><fpage>675</fpage><lpage>688</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9043143</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Noormohammadi</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Markham</surname><given-names>PF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanci</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Whithear</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name><name><surname>Browning</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A novel mechanism for control of antigenic variation in the haemagglutinin gene family of <italic>Mycoplasma synoviae</italic></article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>911</fpage><lpage>923</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10692167</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2958.2000.01766.x</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>